    "evidence_text": "We conduct this model on the MovieQA dataset using Plot Synopses only, and achieve 79.99% accuracy which is the state of the art on the dataset.\n\nLastly, our model reaches 79.99% accuracy on the MovieQA dataset which yields top 1 result on this dataset.\n\nExperimental Result\tWe mainly focus on the MovieQA dataset to train and evaluate our model.\n\nMovieQA dataset aims to evaluate automatic story comprehension from both video and text.\n\nThis challenging dataset is suitable to evaluate QACNN because movie plots are longer than normal reading comprehension task.\n\nEach question comes with a set of five highly plausible choices, only one of which is correct; In the MovieQA benchmark, there are 1958 QA pairs in the val set and\n\nWe also applied our model to MCTest dataset which requires machines to answer multiple-choice reading comprehension questions about fictional stories.\n\nBecause of the restricted training set and development set, we trained our model on MovieQA training set and applied the result to test MCTest dataset.\n\nIn this experiment, our target is to validate the effect of query-based attention in QACNN.\n\nThe power of the model is verified on MovieQA dataset, which yielded the\n\nstate of the art result on the dataset.",
